source: crates/hydronode-cli/tests/c3_help.rs
expression: text
---
Change firmware, send interval, power mode or add the WiFi signal value on one
or more devices. HydroNode checks every device first; you see what changes and
confirm. Devices that cannot take the change are skipped.

Usage: hn devices update [OPTIONS] <SENSORS>...

Arguments:
  <SENSORS>...  Sensor ids (1 to 200)

Options:
      --firmware <VERSION>   Firmware version or "latest"
      --interval <SPAN>      Send interval (10s to 7d)
      --power <POWER>        Power mode [possible values: always-on, modem-sleep, light-sleep, deep-sleep, hibernate]
      --add-rssi             Also send the WiFi signal (RSSI)
      --verify <VERIFY>      How the device proves the update worked [possible values: strict, ingest]
      --confirm-low-battery  Go ahead for devices below 30 % battery too
  -y, --yes                  Do not ask
  -h, --help                 Print help

Global options:
  -p, --profile <NAME>  Profile to use (server and login), see 'hn profile list'
      --json            Print JSON instead of tables (stable shape, for scripts)

Examples:
  hn devices update <sensor-id> --firmware latest
  hn devices update <id> <id> --interval 5m
  hn devices update <sensor-id> --power deep-sleep --yes
